# Python bytecode caches (build artifacts — never source)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Sim run artifacts (task-075). Every `runstore.py capture` writes one JSON
# here plus an index entry — volatile local output, not a record. Promoting a
# result into the committed record is a deliberate act (`capture --publish`),
# which writes docs/sim/runs/published/<experiment>.json — that IS committed,
# and is the artifact a design conversation may cite.
#
# The trailing /* is load-bearing, not a typo for `docs/sim/runs/`: git will
# not descend into an excluded DIRECTORY, so a plain `docs/sim/runs/` makes
# the `!` line below unreachable and silently ignores published/ too
# (verified with `git check-ignore -v`). Excluding the directory's ENTRIES
# instead leaves published/ re-includable.
docs/sim/runs/*
!docs/sim/runs/published/

# Paca API credentials — never commit
Scripts/.paca.json

# Ad-hoc MCP/PIE capture scratch dropped next to the scripts that made it.
# Evidence worth keeping goes to docs/perf/evidence/, not here.
Scripts/shot-*.png
Scripts/snap*.json
Scripts/snap*.txt
Scripts/slate-snapshot.txt
_to_delete/
